.TH WGTUI 1 "2026" "wgtui" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wgtui \- manage remote WireGuard servers over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wgtui
.RI [ command " [" args ... ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wgtui
is a terminal UI and CLI for managing one or more remote WireGuard servers over
plain SSH \- no agent, no web UI, no extra open port on the server.
.PP
Run with no arguments to launch the interactive terminal UI. Any subcommand
runs the non-interactive CLI instead, suitable for scripting.
.PP
Every command that reaches the network prompts interactively for the SSH
and/or sudo password if key/agent authentication isn't enough.
.B wgtui
never accepts a password via a command-line argument or an environment
variable.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "server add " id " \-\-ssh\-host " host " [\-\-ssh\-user " user "] [\-\-ssh\-port " port "] [\-\-ssh\-identity " path "] [\-\-display\-name " name "]"
Register a new server in the local vault.
.TP
.BI "server inspect " id " [\-\-json]"
Connect and run read-only discovery: OS, WireGuard install state,
interfaces, network/firewall state.
.TP
.BI "server install\-wireguard " id " [\-\-yes]"
Install WireGuard on a server that doesn't have it yet.
.TP
.BI "server configure " id " [\-\-interface " wg0 "] [\-\-vpn\-cidr " cidr "] [\-\-port " 51820 "] [\-\-outbound\-interface " if "] [\-\-full\-tunnel\-default=false] [\-\-yes]"
Guided first-time WireGuard interface setup.
.TP
.BI "peer list " id " [\-\-json]"
List a server's peers, reconciled with local metadata.
.TP
.BI "peer add " id " \-\-name " name " [\-\-full\-tunnel | \-\-split\-tunnel " cidrs "] [\-\-keepalive " N "] [\-\-dns " ips "] [\-\-endpoint\-host " host "] [\-\-no\-psk] [\-\-output " path "] [\-\-qr] [\-\-show] [\-\-yes] [\-\-json]"
Add a new peer: generates a client keypair locally, allocates a VPN
address, and produces a ready-to-import client profile.
.TP
.BI "peer disable " id " " peer-name " [\-\-yes]"
Pause a peer: removed from runtime and persistent config, kept locally
so it can be resumed.
.TP
.BI "peer enable " id " " peer-name " [\-\-yes]"
Resume a peer previously disabled.
.TP
.BI "peer revoke " id " " peer-name " [\-\-delete\-profile] [\-\-delete\-metadata] [\-\-yes]"
Revoke a peer's server access. Deleting the local profile or metadata are
separate, explicit choices.
.TP
.BI "peer rotate " id " " peer-name " [\-\-yes]"
Replace a peer's keypair in a single atomic change.
.TP
.BI "peer export " id " " peer-name " \-\-output " path " [\-\-force]"
Write a peer's stored client profile to a file.
.TP
.BI "peer import " id " \-\-file " path " \-\-name " name " [\-\-interface " if "]"
Register an existing local \fB.conf\fR as a managed peer, after verifying
its public key is actually present on the server.
.TP
.BI "diagnose " id " [\-\-json]"
Run the diagnostic checklist: reachability, WireGuard tooling,
interface/config drift, forwarding, firewall backend, peer key age.
.TP
.B mcp
Run as an MCP server over stdio, exposing server/peer operations as
tools for AI agent front ends. Requires
.B WGTUI_MASTER_PASSWORD
to be set, since there is no terminal to prompt on; see
.I docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
in the source tree.
.TP
.BI "completion " "bash|zsh|fish"
Print a shell completion script for the given shell.
.TP
.B version
Print the running version, and a notice if a newer release is available
(this never triggers an automatic update).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/wgtui/vault.json
The encrypted local vault: registered servers, peer metadata, and saved
client profiles. Protected by a master password set on first run, in
addition to filesystem permissions.
.SH SECURITY
.B wgtui
never sends a private key to the server it manages, and never accepts a
password as a process argument or environment variable. See
.I docs/THREAT_MODEL.md
in the source tree for the full analysis.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full specification and architecture docs in the project source tree under
.IR docs/ .
